values
  (210, 'How slice 3.3 is built (`slice-3-3.md`), from G14 and 178. Tasks come from one provider, set by `TASK_PROVIDER`: `builtin` (the default, needing no credential) or `jira`, read through Jira''s REST API with a credential of the API''s own (`JIRA_BASE_URL`, `JIRA_EMAIL`, `JIRA_API_TOKEN`, `JIRA_PROJECT_KEY`, default `SCRUM`), never cached and never given to the agent. A task is its key, title, status (todo, doing, done), assignee, link and last change. Built-in tasks are created and edited by a signed-in person on the version they saw, with their history. The teammate links a thread to one task (`link_task`), and records and ends waits (`record_wait`, `end_wait`): who waits on whom, for what, since when and where, the waiter having written in the thread; at most ten open per thread; posted with the person waited on mentioned. A person may record their own wait and end one they are part of in the web app', 'Unset configuration keeps the feature working without a credential. One home per kind of content (rule 5 of `wave-2.md`) means the two providers are never synced. Recording only waits stated by someone in the thread keeps the list from filling with the model''s guesses', 'active', 'the owner', '2026-11-25T00:00:00Z', 'import', '210')
on conflict (origin, origin_ref) where origin_ref is not null do nothing;
